          <h2 style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:1.1rem;font-weight:700;margin-bottom:0.75rem;margin-top:1.25rem">Tips for shopping sales and avoiding discount traps</h2>
          <ul style="color:var(--muted);font-size:0.9rem;line-height:2;padding-left:1.5rem">
            <li><strong>Check the original price:</strong> Some retailers inflate prices before a sale. Check price history tools to verify the original price was genuine.</li>
            <li><strong>Compare per unit:</strong> A larger pack at a lower percentage discount may be cheaper per unit than a smaller pack with a bigger discount.</li>
            <li><strong>Stack discounts carefully:</strong> If you apply a 20% discount code on top of a 30% sale, you don't get 50% off. You get 30% off, then 20% off the reduced price — which equals 44% total.</li>
            <li><strong>VAT and tax:</strong> In the UK and EU, displayed prices include VAT. In the USA, sales tax is added at checkout — always check whether the discount applies before or after tax.</li>
